### lesson6 manual endpoint tests (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client — just hit Run)
@host = http://localhost:8080
@user = Anyname

### Connectivity check
GET {{host}}/hello-world-bean

### Path variable
GET {{host}}/hello-world/path-variable/Zhongyan

### List
GET {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos

### Single item
GET {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos/1

### Single item — nonexistent id, should be 404 and not 500
GET {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos/99999

### Someone else's todo — should be 404; you must not see other people's data
GET {{host}}/users/SomeoneElse/todos/1

### Create — should be 201, with a Location header and the backend-assigned id in the body
POST {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": -1,
  "description": "Learn REST properly",
  "targetDate": "2026-12-31",
  "done": false
}

### Create — description too short, should be 400 with a message in the body
POST {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": -1,
  "description": "abc",
  "targetDate": "2026-12-31",
  "done": false
}

### Update — note that the id in the body is ignored; the path wins
PUT {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 99,
  "description": "Learn Angular Components - updated",
  "targetDate": "2027-01-15",
  "done": true
}

### Delete — should be 204 with no response body
DELETE {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos/1

### Delete again — should be 404
DELETE {{host}}/users/{{user}}/todos/1
